              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "periūrium, periūriī — \"perjury, a false oath\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Periūrium grave crīmen erat. Perjury was a serious crime."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, from periūrus, 'oath-breaking': per- here means 'wrongly'. English perjury."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "periūrium is built on periūrus, \"oath-breaking\" (EtymDB), from per-, here \"wrongly\", and the root of iūrō, \"to swear\". English perjury comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
