              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arguō, arguere — \"to prove; to accuse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Haec epistula eum mentītum esse arguit. This letter proves that he lied."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arguō, arguere, arguī, argūtum: to make clear, and so to prove or to charge. English argue."
            }
          ]
        },
