          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "arguō first meant \"to make clear\"; Lewis & Short connect it with the root of argentum, \"silver\", and Greek argos, \"bright\". English argue comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
